Fits of C(T) (w=2 rows):
  C ~    61.60 * const     rel-rms residual = 0.258
  C ~   126.73 * rho(T)    rel-rms residual = 0.161
  C ~    12.82 * logT      rel-rms residual = 0.152
  C ~     4.73 * sqrtT     rel-rms residual = 0.212

registered reading: the basis with smallest rel-rms is the C(T) law; if rho(T) wins and
C/rho is flat across BOTH widths, then R ~ rho(T)/w^2 = (Weyl zero density)/w^2 — the
structure-side count tied a-priori to the zero density. Flat C/rho is the deliverable.
